There is a lack of distinction between the voiceless [[Alveolar consonant|alveolar]] consonant /t/ and the voiceless [[Velar consonant|velar]] consonant /k/ in spoken Vilela. For example, in the word [huanokol] 'dog',<ref>{{Cite web |title=Vilela Words|url=https://www.native-languages.org/vilela_words.htm|access-date=2026-04-13|website=www.native-languages.org}}</ref> [k] could be pronounced as /k/ or /t/. The sounds may even [[Alternation (linguistics)|alternate]] within the same word. This alternation appears to occur not only in casual speech, but also in formal speech. Although this alternation occurs, [k] tends to predominate.<ref name=":02">{{Cite journal |last=Golluscio|first=Lucía|title=¿Lengua o hablante?–Investigando las alternancias coronal-velares en vilela|url=https://www.researchgate.net/publication/268806700_Lengua_o_hablante_-_Investigando_las_alternancias_coronal-velares_en_vilela|journal=LIAMES Línguas Indígenas Americanas|volume=14|issue=1|pages=41-72|via=ResearchGate|last2=Grawunder|first2=Sven|date=May 2014}}</ref>

Open Language Archives Community (OLAC) has approximately 34 audio logs of the Vilela language being spoken in interviews. The audio logs consist of numbers, commands, and other aspects of the spoken language.<ref>{{Cite web |title=OLAC resources in and about the Vilela language|url=http://www.language-archives.org/language/vil|access-date=2026-03-30|website=www.language-archives.org}}</ref>

==Typology==
The Vilela language is described as a head-marking language, meaning that the grammatical relationship is addressed at the beginning of the sentence rather than the start of the sentence focusing on the dependents.<ref name=":0">{{Cite journal |last=Golluscio|first=Lucía|title=¿Lengua o hablante?–Investigando las alternancias coronal-velares en vilela|url=https://www.researchgate.net/publication/268806700_Lengua_o_hablante_-_Investigando_las_alternancias_coronal-velares_en_vilela|journal=LIAMES Línguas Indígenas Americanas|volume=14|issue=1|pages=41-72|via=ResearchGate|last2=Grawunder|first2=Sven|date=May 2014}}</ref> 

